A||||6||JetroGT||Taking a Trip in the Fiero||||6||
Z||000000||JetroGT||03-14-2001||12:30 AM||||This Friday I'm driving back up to Kenosha Wisconsin. Monday I had the trans and engine oil changed along with a 4-wheel alingment. That should be good enough. I'm going to drive straight through. It's only about 1000 miles. I'm driving up 35 through Oklahoma city. After that it should be a straight shot to Chicago. Any Fiero shows along the way? Any way, I hope I make it! The car is an 86 SE pushing 130,000 miles!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/JetroGTsig.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000001||Cheever2||03-14-2001||12:47 AM||||My map/direction thing says 1,034 miles, over 17 hours.  At about 291 miles or 7 hours, you'll pass by my hometown of Tulsa, but I don't know any Fieros there.  You probably won't be tired enough by that time to require any assistance from my brother.  But give a salute to Route 66 when you cross it.  Safe journey, guy.<P> ||||reg||6
Z||000002||Roy Grooms||03-14-2001||06:17 PM|||| GOOD LUCK,I made about a 1500 mile trip last year ya , from K,TOWM WI. TO N.C. through the smokies and around the state,had <BR>a great time like you I drove my toy, (84 fiero) wow what fun the toy has been reworked from brakes to shocks ,it a auto trans did the oil change thing and lube,check it all over and had NO problem at all when you get back e mail me i live in Trevor WI. ROYBOY@HOTMAIL.COM<BR>   (ROYSTOY)||||reg||10
Z||000003||KissMySSFiero||03-14-2001||06:55 PM||||hey i just made a 1100 mile trip in my formula pulling a uhaul trailer.  right now im at about 150000 miles and i had no problems whatsoever.  my cruising speed was about 75 most of the way and sometimes i looked down and was goin OVER 100mph.  that was goin down the mountains though.  didnt want to do that long..   <P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:KissMySSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>   <A HREF="mailto:KissMySSFiero@netzero.net">KissMySSFiero@netzero.net</A>    <P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">        <BR>"There's a fine line between love and beer"||||reg||1
Z||000004||JetroGT||03-17-2001||09:45 PM||||Well, I made it! No problems. I left at 2:15pm and arrived at 7am. Through Oklahoma I was crusing at about 75-80. Then I got into Missouri and it started to get cold. I stopped at a truck stop to call my parents and noticed frost on peoples windshields. And going through St. Louis I stayed at about 55-60 MPH. I saw about 5 cops and 3 of them had people pulled over. When I crossed the Mississippi and into Ill. it started snow. It kept snowing untill I got to Kenosha. Which made the ride a little longer. <P>I was coming up 55 and  my radar detector kept going off. I coulden't see where it was coming from. And then I came around a bend and saw about 12 cop cars around a smashed Duster, or Corssica. It was hard to tell. And a big Semi/w trailer in the ditch. Who ever was in that car must have died. After I saw that I stayed behind a semi untill the roads looked a little better. <BR>I hope I have better weather on the way back!||||reg||14
Z||000005||Cheever2||03-17-2001||09:56 PM||||Glad that wasn't you in the ditch.  Sounds like a pretty good trip otherwise.  Thanks for the update.  <BR>BTW, where were the worst roads (I mean potholes, etc)?<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000006||JetroGT||03-27-2001||04:27 AM||||Now I'm back in Texas. On the way back I took a detour. I almost got to St. Louis when I decided to check out The Fiero Factory. I took 24 through Kentucky and Tennessee. Then down 65 from Nashville. When I got their they were closed. Oh well. They were probably in Daytona or just not open on Sunday. I took a few pictures any way! Then I drove down to Birmingham on 65 untill that met up with 2059. then hwy 20 all the way back to Fort Worth. That was a long Drive!<BR>Total trip milage was 3061 miles! I got home yesterday around 2:30 in the morning. All in all it was a good trip. Next time I want to drive the 5spd. <P>The worst roads were in Illinois, Northern Illinois. You would think that with all the tolls that the roads would be in better shape. <p>[This message has been edited by JetroGT (edited 03-27-2001).]||||reg||14
